  autumn_160x120 — 99,896 misses, 1.3 s miss wall:
    zlib/atlas-*     : 34,944 execs, 8,736 distinct each, 651.6 ms (51.3%)
      — 100% exhausted, 0 stored
    zlib/law-lattice : 16,320, 15,520 distinct, 282.0 ms (22.2%) — exhausted
    zstd3/law-lattice: 16,072, 15,520 distinct, 100.2 ms (7.9%) — 3.54 MiB
  gradient_320x240 — same shape (rows in the run log), smaller shares.

Findings (arithmetic through tools):
  1. THE REMAINING MASS IS THE EXPENSIVE CLASS AND IT IS UNSTORED. On
     screenshot, the two zlib atlas families are 87.4% of the executed-
     miss wall with ZERO stored bytes; first-come-first-served admission
     fills the 8 MiB body budget with cheaper zstd3 families (whose
     probes already run at 2.4-2.6 us reused) before the ~10-23 us zlib
     bodies arrive. The census quantifies displacement, not just scarcity.
  2. COMPUTATIONAL VALUE PER MiB (Jon's D3 objective): covering the zlib
     atlas distinct sets (6,609 x 2 x ~938 B = 11.8 MiB on screenshot)
     would avoid 5,134 ms of measured miss mass = ~434 ms/MiB; autumn
     41.7 ms/MiB (15.6 MiB / 652 ms). The displaced zstd3 law-lattice
     mass runs 11.9 ms per stored MiB remaining (screenshot) — the
     current allocation captures the LOW-value side of the frontier.
  3. Repeats-per-distinct on the screenshot atlas families: 254,848 /
     6,609 = ~38.6x — matching D0's redundancy thesis, now priced.
  4. The stopping criterion is MET: a measurable cost concentration
     exists (zlib class, ~51-87% of remaining miss mass, 0 stored).
     Whether a D3-B arm clears the complexity bar is a separate call:
     measured ceiling on the corpus walls is a few seconds on Maximum
     (e.g. ~1.7 s of ~414.5 s on screenshot's share at 4 MiB reallocated)
     — small against the P1 ladder, concentrated in one class.

Gates this exercise:
  fmt + clippy -D warnings green; release suite (D3 census in the
  ignored set); verify chain (corpus digests + RSS) and fuzz rerun post-
  instrument; D3-B arms NOT run (budget frozen per instruction; B1/B2/B3
  designs recorded in [mnf15-p1d-record](mnf15-p1d-record.md) as future
  work with the measured frontier above).

D3-A atlas invariants (source-level dependency analysis, next steps):
  atlas probe body = pack(residual(tile.data - transform(ref_rgb(prior))))
  — depends on (tile.data, prior CONTENT, transform, planar). Prior
  content = the atlas insertion history (position-dependent through the
  upstream tiles' pixels), so D1b-style whole-decision memoization of
  the atlas segment needs atlas-state in its key and is NOT a pure
  function of tile bytes — unlike the laws lattice. The measured repeat
  structure (6,609 distinct bodies across half a million executions)
  makes BODY-level and cross-sweep reuse the exact-safe surface; a
  decision-lattice memo would require an exact atlas-state identity
  test first. Recorded as the open D3-A question for the next stage.
Wire: untouched. Decoder: untouched. Budgets: frozen.
